/Users/enzo/.claude/projects/-Users-enzo-harness-lumos-toolchain/26a6b57a-9efc-4073-b845-c27e42a2fbb1.jsonl:13197:{"parentUuid":"2215680b-1b89-4639-97c7-69f7956a4fad","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e1b22e58-418e-447a-bcbb-888775122127","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011WAYsjG2hPfPgMKb8rVvkK","type":"tool_result","content":"# Stop Hook Decision Control\n\n## Can Stop Block?\n\nYes. According to the exit code behavior table:\n\n> `Stop` | Yes | Prevents Claude from stopping, continues the conversation\n\n## JSON Decision Control for Stop\n\nThe Stop hook supports the following decision control via JSON output:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"decision\": \"block\",\n  \"reason\": \"Custom reason why Claude should continue\"\n}\n```\n\nReturning this JSON with exit code 0 will prevent Claude from stopping and show the reason to Claude.\n\nFrom the documentation:\n\n> Return `decision: \"block\"` with an optional `reason` to prevent Claude from stopping. The reason appears to Claude as context for continuing the conversation.\n\n## Stop Hook Input Fields\n\nThe Stop hook receives the following documented input fields:\n\n| Field | Description |\n|:------|:------------|\n| `stop_hook_active` | Boolean indicating whether the Stop hook can actually block. Set to `false` if you don't have permission to block stops, such as in `dontAsk` mode |\n| `transcript_path` | Path to conversation JSON |\n| `session_id` | Current session identifier |\n\nAdditionally, Stop hooks receive all [common input fields](#common-input-fields) like `cwd`, `permission_mode`, `hook_event_name`, and `last_assistant_message`.\n\nThe `stop_hook_active` field is critical: you should only attempt to block if it's `true`. When it's `false`, your block decision will be ignored."}]},"uuid":"bf66f414-7048-4627-9e4c-2f4c6c5277e6","timestamp":"2026-09-05T03:57:06.784Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":317647,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Stop Hook Decision Control\n\n## Can Stop Block?\n\nYes. According to the exit code behavior table:\n\n> `Stop` | Yes | Prevents Claude from stopping, continues the conversation\n\n## JSON Decision Control for Stop\n\nThe Stop hook supports the following decision control via JSON output:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"decision\": \"block\",\n  \"reason\": \"Custom reason why Claude should continue\"\n}\n```\n\nReturning this JSON with exit code 0 will prevent Claude from stopping and show the reason to Claude.\n\nFrom the documentation:\n\n> Return `decision: \"block\"` with an optional `reason` to prevent Claude from stopping. The reason appears to Claude as context for continuing the conversation.\n\n## Stop Hook Input Fields\n\nThe Stop hook receives the following documented input fields:\n\n| Field | Description |\n|:------|:------------|\n| `stop_hook_active` | Boolean indicating whether the Stop hook can actually block. Set to `false` if you don't have permission to block stops, such as in `dontAsk` mode |\n| `transcript_path` | Path to conversation JSON |\n| `session_id` | Current session identifier |\n\nAdditionally, Stop hooks receive all [common input fields](#common-input-fields) like `cwd`, `permission_mode`, `hook_event_name`, and `last_assistant_message`.\n\nThe `stop_hook_active` field is critical: you should only attempt to block if it's `true`. When it's `false`, your block decision will be ignored.","durationMs":6042,"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2215680b-1b89-4639-97c7-69f7956a4fad","session_id":"1eeb5654-5918-4030-95d1-6723f6b0923f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/enzo/harness/lumos-toolchain","sessionId":"26a6b57a-9efc-4073-b845-c27e42a2fbb1","version":"2.1.260","gitBranch":"main","slug":"luminous-skipping-marble"}
