 it in the SAME hook result as the rewrite \u2014 it is then dropped automatically if your rewrite is rejected or superseded by a later hook's rewrite; assertions returned without a rewrite are never invalidated by other hooks' rewrites, so a non-rewriting hook should assert only what holds regardless of other hooks' rewrites \u2014 hosts that need an assertion bound to exact output bytes should make it in the hook that produces those bytes. (Do NOT return an identity rewrite just to pair an assertion: hooks run in parallel on the ORIGINAL output, so an identity rewrite competes last-write-wins with sibling rewrites and can clobber a real redaction.)"),updatedToolOutput:se().optional().describe("Replaces the tool output before it is sent to the model"),updatedMCPToolOutput:se().optional().describe("Replaces the output for MCP tools only. Prefer updatedToolOutput, which works for all tools")})),Cie=m(()=>c({hookEventName:k("PostToolBatch"),additionalContext:s().optional()})),Oie=m(()=>c({hookEventName:k("PostToolUseFailure"),additionalContext:s().optional()})),kie=m(()=>c({hookEventName:k("Stop"),additionalContext:s().optional()}).describe("Hook-specific output for the Stop event. additionalContext is non-error feedback delivered to the model; the conversation continues so the model can act on it.")),wie=m(()=>c({hookEventName:k("SubagentStop"),additionalContext:s().optional()}).describe("Hook-specific output for the SubagentStop event. additionalContext is non-error feedback delivered to the subagent; the subagent continues so it can act on it.")),Mie=m(()=>c({hookEventName:k("PermissionDenied"),retry:O().optional()})),Iie=m(()=>c({hookEventName:k("Notification"),additionalContext:s().optional()})),Die=m(()=>c({hookEventName:k("PermissionRequest"),decision:$e([c({behavior:k("allow"),updatedInput:fe(s(),se()).optional(),updatedPermissions:v(Ti()).optional()}),c({behavior:k("deny"),message:s().optional(),interrupt:O().optional()})])})),xie=m(()=>c({hookEventName:k("Cw